## Print / diagnostic catalog extensions

- GET|POST /api/admin/diagnostic-catalog/imaging-phrases, PATCH|DELETE .../[id]
- GET /api/imaging-phrases (ops phrase picker)
- Analyte section / valueType / AnalyteValueOption via analytes admin API
- GET `/api/admin/diagnostic-catalog/analyte-dictionary?q=` — unscoped `AnalyteDictionary` search. Add-analyte modal fills the form from it. Seed: `prisma/seed-data/analyte-dictionary.json` via `db:seed` / `db:seed:diagnostic-catalog:base` (rebuild with `node prisma/scripts/build-analyte-dictionary.mjs`)
- ADR: docs/adr/clinic-print-forms.md
- Patient card (modal and `/patients/[id]`) uses a stay strip plus tabs Guest / Doctor / Diagnostics / Plan / Package. Sanatorium row icons open the same card on Guest, Plan, Package, or Diagnostics (package courses).
- Procedure sheet (`/print/procedures/[patientId]`) lists `SCHEDULED`, `CHECKED_IN`, `COMPLETED`, and `NO_SHOW`, plus seated/`PLAN_BEFORE_PAY` unpaid extras when the org route shows them on plan. Names follow the print language from the service catalog. The date row is gray on paper. Body sites and device settings print in the Notes column. Shared A4 header: one-line date plus patient (left) and episode stay (right). `HOLD_UNTIL_PAY` unseated extras and `PROPOSED` rows stay off the sheet. OPEN day-buckets (CLI-62) print at end of day with an open-attendance label instead of a wall clock until nurse seats a cabin. Print routes render without the viewport shell so the sheet is not clipped to one page. Extra-procedure payment print is a 58 mm roll (`/print/extra-ticket/[ticketId]`) with a Baku issue stamp, line total, hotel room label, a signature box, and the ticket id at the foot. Lab result print (`/print/lab-order/[id]`) lists every panel analyte in catalog order, including an empty value, with unit and flag columns.
- Package assign asks for a start day and hour before seating new lines. Other seating paths (confirm, paid extra, replace) start at the next open hour and snap to the 5-minute grid. A miss says whether staff are missing, staff or the cabin are busy, the day is at its procedure cap, or a rule blocks the slot.
- Print checkup (`/print/checkup/[patientId]`) includes episode ICD diagnoses (`print-checkup.service`); default sections = Nafta intake 4 (`therapist` / `gynecologist` / `cardiologist` / `usm`)
- Course summary (`/print/episode/[patientId]?episode=`) — stay + anamnesis + complaints + ICD + labs (all items) + exam notes + seated procedures (`print-episode-summary.service`). Printer on the patient-card stay strip. OPEN prints with an interim note.
- Visit exam print: `/print/visit-exam/[cpoeEntryId]` (`print-visit-exam.service`) — one `CpoeEntry`; whole-visit / FHIR = future debt
- Patient card `GET /api/patients/[id]/card-summary` → `intakeChecklist` lists auto analyses, auto diagnostics, and auto doctor visits from the current package template after the first care-team doctor. A visit row books a time onto the existing visit (`POST /api/visits/[id]/appointment`). It does not use a fixed four-slot Nafta list and does not wait for `ProgramInstance`. Live: `applyPackageAutoBlocks`. Opening a course does not create orders. The first care-team doctor (`CARE_TEAM`) books every `AUTO_ON_OPEN` and `AUTO_DAY1` block from the current template even when `ProgramInstance` does not exist yet. `MANUAL_RETRY` (super-admin refresh) moves the course onto the current package version, recomputes quotas, cancels excess future planned sessions from the end of the stay, then creates missing auto visits and labs. Bulk: `POST /api/sanatorium/package-apply-open` (platform super-admin, OPEN courses with a program only). ECG/USG blocks marked Auto book `CARDIO-ECG` / `USG-ABD`. Card: anamnesis, complaints, ICD-10, and that checklist after the first doctor; the package itself opens only when anamnesis, one complaint, and one ICD-10 are all present; package procedures and schedule use the same three gates; results and exam notes only when they have rows.
- POST|DELETE /api/sanatorium/episodes/[id]/confirm-no-package — ops signal «guest has no package»; DELETE undoes it, and a new `ProgramInstance` clears it automatically
- POST /api/sanatorium/episodes/[id]/package-apply — super-admin: current template version, quota shrink, then missing auto visits/labs
- POST /api/sanatorium/package-apply-open — same apply for every OPEN course that already has a program
- GET|POST /api/sanatorium/episodes/[id]/bath-calendar — kept for recalc/debug. The package modal has no mini calendar. Saxla seats day-series baths with `defaultBathMode` (Nafta `3`): naftalan first, iodine/hydro on empty days. The clock uses the same minute grid as other procedures (guest rest + cabin). Closed-day rest flags and `weeklyNaftalanCap` are clinic settings. Opposite-sex SKUs are refused at assign. A miss names the procedure and the day; seated siblings stay. Citizenship labels use kit `countryLabel` az/en/ru.
- POST /api/admin/schedule-recalc — super-admin preview or apply of the stay graph after a clinic-day change. Apply reseats moved rows through the minute grid; it does not slam 09:00.
- POST /api/admin/schedule-reseat — super-admin preview or apply: future `SCHEDULED` on one episode, all overlaps (`allOpenOverlaps`), or rows on closed clinic days (`allOpenClosedDays`). Closed-day rows pin to the next working day from `listClinicDays` (week template is SoR). The minute grid uses the same closed set. Not a table wipe. Not the stay-tail recalc.
- POST /api/admin/clinic-days — open or close one civil day
- GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE /api/admin/lab-blank-profiles — panel list plus Word blank. The blank's `serviceCode` is the panel code. POST with `id` or the same panel code updates that blank. PATCH `/api/admin/lab-blank-profiles/[id]` sets `active`. POST /api/lab-orders/[id]/blank reads a filled `.docx` only when that panel has an active blank.
- Cutover report: `scripts/nafta-cutover/rebuild-intake.cjs` (cards `slices.diagnostics`); map `src/lib/import/nafta-intake-map.ts`

## ICD-10 catalog (CLI-39…42)

Global WHO ICD-10 (2019) table `IcdCode` — **no** `organizationId`. Search `GET /api/icd` (selectable CATEGORY/LEAF only; not `/api/icd10`). ADR: [clinic-icd10-catalog.md](../../../docs/adr/clinic-icd10-catalog.md). Optional sync from orchestrator `GET /platform/v1/catalog/icd10` (in-process, not data-hub). Data = original sources only (`packages/satellite-kit/icd10/catalog.cjs`, `sources/SOURCES.md`); missing RU/AZ titles are `NULL` → `icdTitle` fallback. `prisma/load-icd10.cjs` upserts by code, deletes only unreferenced non-catalog rows, never deletes diagnoses.

## Platform billing status

`GET /api/platform/billing-status` — `app/api/platform/billing-status/route.ts` re-exports `@era/satellite-kit/billing/status-route` (banner in `EraAppRouteShell`). Staff calls the orchestrator denies (SOFT_BLOCK export, HARD_BLOCK write) get 402 from kit `readSatelliteStaffSession`; `handleRouteError` returns `{ error, code, billingStatus }`. ADR `docs/adr/billing-enforcement-satellites.md`.
